WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.276
Meet Associate Professor Kwame Lindqvist,

00:00:04.376 --> 00:00:06.906
Director of the Master of Priority Studies.

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:09.236
I started in public finance.

00:00:09.536 --> 00:00:12.886
A priority gets its budget long before it gets a definition,

00:00:13.036 --> 00:00:14.816
and I study what happens in between.

00:00:15.316 --> 00:00:18.076
A tailor promises your clothes back in forty-eight hours,

00:00:18.226 --> 00:00:20.696
and starts the clock later as the work piles up.

00:00:20.996 --> 00:00:24.836
A retail chain's software writes your priority before your review.

00:00:25.136 --> 00:00:27.626
A parking office brings in a new scorecard,

00:00:27.776 --> 00:00:29.816
and much the same people get permits.

00:00:30.416 --> 00:00:33.246
No one in the School of Emergent Priorities is cited more often.

00:00:33.846 --> 00:00:35.610
Two hundred and seven research outputs,

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:38.000
cited one thousand and sixty-eight times.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.660
And an h-index of twenty-eight,

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.170
the highest in his School.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.163
So I tell my students:

00:00:44.363 --> 00:00:45.583
read the budget first.

00:00:45.883 --> 00:00:47.363
The definition comes later.

00:00:48.663 --> 00:00:49.917
Our website has more.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:51.017
Find us on Bluesky,

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:52.057
or email us.
